---
// Counter-measurement IV (capstone) — "Patterns".
// Each day the machine blindly finds the strongest correlation in the house's own Protocol
// archive — and cannot say whether it means anything. Only the permutation test separates signal
// from noise, and even it is fooled by trends. Data: src/data/pattern/latest.json.
//
// Two illustrations left the confession paragraph on 2026-08-22 (currency audit), because the
// archive refutes both. "The sea warms, the ice melts" described the sea-ice ↔ sea-surface-
// temperature pair, which won on 2 of 64 committed days; on the rest the pick was sea ice ↔ world
// population. And "tomorrow it will pair earthquakes with football" advertised a promiscuity the
// instrument does not have: 64 snapshots produced three distinct pairs, 48 of them the same one.
// What stays is the clause that was always true and always load-bearing — this test is fooled by
// trends — now with the reason it is. The open question the audit raised, whether a permutation
// test that has never once fired still carries the work's thesis, is issue #724 and the
// architect's to answer; this page does not answer it in passing.
// Note for the next editor: keep such notes HERE. An HTML comment in the template below ships
// into dist/ and would quote the retired phrasing to every visitor who reads the source.
import { getRelativeLocaleUrl } from 'astro:i18n'
import { t } from '@/i18n/ui'
import type { Locale } from '@/lib/site'
import type { PatternData } from '@/lib/pattern/types'
import { rStr, pct, normalize, linePath } from '@/lib/pattern/format'
import data from '@/data/pattern/latest.json'
import SheetHead from '@/components/experiments/SheetHead.astro'
import SheetFoot from '@/components/experiments/SheetFoot.astro'
import '@/styles/experiment-sheet.css'

interface Props { locale: Locale }
const { locale } = Astro.props
const de = locale === 'de'
const d = data as unknown as PatternData
const h = d.headline
const methodUrl = getRelativeLocaleUrl(locale, '/werke/pattern')

const W = 640
const H = 150
const pathA = linePath(normalize(h.a_series), W, H)
const pathB = linePath(normalize(h.b_series), W, H)
const survives = d.false_discovery_rate < 0.1

// USP rework #15 (program doc 2026-08-09): the null distribution, drawn. The pipeline
// emits it from 2026-08-09 on; older committed data renders the honest placeholder line.
interface NullDist { bins: number; range: [number, number]; counts: number[] }
const nd = (d as { null_distribution?: NullDist }).null_distribution
const ndMax = nd ? Math.max(...nd.counts) : 0
const ndMarkerX = nd ? Math.min(nd.bins * 10 - 1, Math.abs(h.r) * nd.bins * 10) : 0
---

<main id="main" class="flex-1">
<article class="pattern mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14">
  <SheetHead title="Patterns">
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-xl text-fg-muted">{t(locale, 'pt.sub')}</p>
  </SheetHead>

  <section class="mb-8 border-l-2 border-accent/60 pl-5">
    <p class="kicker">{de ? 'Der Fund des Tages' : "Today's discovery"}</p>
    <p class="mt-3 text-[clamp(18px,3vw,26px)] font-semibold leading-snug">
      {h.a_label[locale]} <span class="text-fg-faint">↔</span> {h.b_label[locale]}
    </p>
    <p class="mt-1 font-mono text-sm text-fg-muted">r = {rStr(h.r, locale)} · {de ? `über ${d.days} Tage` : `over ${d.days} days`}</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-12">
    <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} class="w-full overflow-visible" role="img"
      aria-label={de ? 'Zwei normierte Reihen, die sich spiegeln' : 'Two normalised series mirroring each other'}>
      <path d={pathA} fill="none" stroke="rgb(var(--rgb-accent))" stroke-width="1.6" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke" />
      <path d={pathB} fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-dasharray="4 3" class="text-fg-faint" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke" />
    </svg>
    <ul class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-x-5 gap-y-1 font-mono text-[11px] text-fg-faint">
      <li class="flex items-center gap-1.5"><svg width="16" height="2" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="0" y1="1" x2="16" y2="1" stroke="rgb(var(--rgb-accent))" stroke-width="2" /></svg>{h.a_label[locale]}</li>
      <li class="flex items-center gap-1.5"><svg width="16" height="2" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="0" y1="1" x2="16" y2="1" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="4 3" /></svg>{h.b_label[locale]}</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-12 rounded-md border border-line bg-panel panel-raised p-5">
    <p class="kicker">{de ? 'Das Geständnis' : 'The confession'}</p>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
      {de
        ? `Die Maschine verglich ${d.pairs} Paare über ${d.days} Tage. ${d.strong_pairs} davon „korrelieren" (|r| ≥ ${d.strong_threshold}). Sie nahm das stärkste und nannte es einen Fund — ohne die leiseste Ahnung, ob es etwas bedeutet. Sie kann es nicht wissen.`
        : `The machine compared ${d.pairs} pairs over ${d.days} days. ${d.strong_pairs} of them "correlate" (|r| ≥ ${d.strong_threshold}). It took the strongest and called it a discovery — without the faintest idea whether it means anything. It cannot know.`}
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">
      {de
        ? `Nur ein Test trennt Signal von Rauschen: die Daten ${d.permutations.toLocaleString('de-DE')}-mal durchschütteln und zählen, wie oft der Zufall allein ein ebenso starkes Muster erzeugt. Hier: ${pct(d.false_discovery_rate, locale)} der Durchläufe. ${survives ? 'Das macht reinen Zufall unwahrscheinlich — nach diesem Test.' : 'Mit anderen Worten: reines Rauschen — der Zufall produziert das ständig.'} Und selbst dieser Test wird von Trends getäuscht: zwei Reihen, die nur in eine Richtung laufen, bringt kein Durchschütteln auseinander.`
        : `Only one test separates signal from noise: shuffle the data ${d.permutations.toLocaleString('en-GB')} times and count how often chance alone produces a pattern this strong. Here: ${pct(d.false_discovery_rate, locale)} of runs. ${survives ? 'That makes pure chance unlikely — by this test.' : 'In other words, pure noise — chance manufactures this all the time.'} And even this test is fooled by trends: no amount of shuffling pulls apart two series that only ever move one way.`}
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-12 border-t border-line pt-6">
    <p class="kicker">
      {de ? 'Die Null-Verteilung — was der Zufall allein produziert' : 'The null distribution — what chance alone produces'}
    </p>
    <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-x-10 gap-y-3">
      <div>
        <p class="text-2xl font-bold tabular-nums">{d.permutations.toLocaleString(de ? 'de-DE' : 'en-GB')}</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-fg-muted">{de ? 'Durchschüttelungen, Seed = Datum' : 'shuffles, seeded by the date'}</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="text-2xl font-bold tabular-nums">{pct(d.false_discovery_rate, locale)}</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-fg-muted">{de ? 'der Zufalls-Läufe erreichten |r| des Funds' : "of chance runs matched the discovery's |r|"}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    {nd && ndMax > 0 && (
      <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${nd.bins * 10} 46`} class="mt-4 h-16 w-full max-w-xl" role="img"
        aria-label={de
          ? `Histogramm: max|r| über ${d.permutations} gemischte Läufe, Markierung beim echten Fund (|r| = ${rStr(Math.abs(h.r), locale)})`
          : `Histogram: max|r| across ${d.permutations} shuffled runs, marker at the real discovery (|r| = ${rStr(Math.abs(h.r), locale)})`}>
        {nd.counts.map((c, i) => {
          const bh = c === 0 ? 0 : Math.max(1.5, (c / ndMax) * 40)
          return <rect x={i * 10 + 1} y={42 - bh} width={8} height={bh} class="fill-current text-fg-faint" />
        })}
        <line x1={ndMarkerX} x2={ndMarkerX} y1={0} y2={44} stroke="rgb(var(--rgb-accent))" stroke-width="1.5" />
      </svg>
    )}
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-xl font-mono text-[11px] leading-relaxed text-fg-faint">
      {nd
        ? de
          ? 'Balken: die Verteilung der stärksten Korrelation aus jedem gemischten Lauf. Die Linie: der echte Fund. Das ist der Unterschied zu Vigens statischem p-Wert — hier steht die ganze Resampling-Verteilung, nachrechenbar aus committeten Daten.'
          : "Bars: the distribution of the strongest correlation in each shuffled run. The line: the real discovery. This is the difference from Vigen's static p-value — the whole resampling distribution, recomputable from committed data."
        : de
          ? 'Für diesen Tag hat die Pipeline keine Verteilung mitgeschrieben — dann steht nur die Rate, ehrlich.'
          : 'For this day the pipeline recorded no distribution — then only the rate stands, honestly.'}
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-10">
    <p class="leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">
      {de
        ? 'Mit genug Reihen und genug Vergleichen findet man immer ein Muster. Das ist die Maschine hinter jeder „datengetriebenen Erkenntnis" — und der blinde Fleck dieses Labs selbst.'
        : 'With enough series and enough comparisons, you always find a pattern. That is the engine behind every "data-driven insight" — and the blind spot of this lab itself.'}
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-12 border-t border-line pt-6">
    <p class="kicker">
      {de ? 'Nächste Nachbarn' : 'Nearest neighbors'}
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">
      {de
        ? 'Diesen Witz macht bereits '
        : 'This exact joke already runs at '}
      <a href="https://tylervigen.com/spurious-correlations" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" class="underline decoration-line underline-offset-2 hover:text-fg">Tyler Vigen, Spurious Correlations</a>
      {de
        ? ' — seit 2014 (Relaunch Januar 2024), die kanonische Referenz: eine Maschine, die autonom ihre eigene Datenbank durcheinandermischt, die stärkste Korrelation zeigt, als „Entdeckung" präsentiert und sich mit einem expliziten Kausalitäts-Vorbehalt selbst unterminiert.'
        : ' — running since 2014 (relaunched January 2024), the canonical reference: a machine that autonomously mines its own database, surfaces the strongest correlation, presents it as a "discovery" and undercuts itself with an explicit spurious-correlation caveat.'}
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">
      {de
        ? 'Der eine reale Unterschied: Vigen zeigt einen statischen p-Wert, diese Seite rechnet tatsächlich einen Permutationstest — tausende Durchmischungen, eine echte Falsch-Entdeckungsrate für genau dieses Paar an genau diesem Tag. Diese Nulldistribution ist die eigentliche Sache; sie beantwortet Vigens Witz mit der Rechenstrenge, die er selbst nicht anlegt.'
        : "The one real difference: Vigen shows a static p-value, this page actually runs a permutation test — thousands of shuffles, a real false-discovery rate for this exact pair on this exact day. That null distribution is the actual point — it answers Vigen's joke with the statistical rigor his own site doesn't apply."}
    </p>
  </section>

  <SheetFoot>
    <p class="font-mono text-xs text-fg-faint">
      {de ? 'Quelle: ' : 'Source: '}{d.source.name}. {de ? `${d.metrics_count} variierende Metriken.` : `${d.metrics_count} varying metrics.`}
    </p>
    <nav class="mt-2">
      <a href={methodUrl} class="sheet-link">{t(locale, 'prot.method')} →</a>
    </nav>
  </SheetFoot>
</article>
</main>
